Z||000000||rockcrawl||08-15-2000||07:35 PM||||It seems like there are a lot of Fiero owners interested in a side scoop that is easy to install and inexpensive. Let me know what you think of this new scoop I designed. I should have the mold done next week, then I can start producing these on an as-needed basis. The picture shows the finished "plug", unpainted. the actual scoop will be cut out where this one is just blacked out with tape. <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.host.bay-town.com/imgdir/966358912-5930.jpg">  <P>more pictures at: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/ss2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/ss2.jpg</A>   <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/ss3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/ss3.jpg</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 08-15-2000).]||||reg||14
