Z||000022||mbramble||08-16-2000||04:25 PM||||Personally, looking at this particular scoop, can't imagine why it wouldn't fit on either side.  Since it just mounts to the existing body panel, and is symmetrical in shape, what would be the difference??  <P>Panels that must have a mirror image to fit the other side are the body/panel scoops that take the place of the original body panel, or are cut to the shape of the panel area.  ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Pontiaddict||08-16-2000||04:53 PM||||MBRAMBLE, you would have to make a mirror image of it because it "leans" in one direction if you put it on the other side, you would have to flip it over and it would then "lean" in the other direction.<BR>If you are still going to try and make some bigger ones yourself, add louvers to it so they look sort of like the ones on the IMSA body kit.<P><BR>Rockcrawl, If you also added louvers to yours, they might cover the indentation and make it look even on both sides. That's if you do make one for the other side.<BR>PS. It looks great as is.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Terrible Tom||08-16-2000||05:11 PM||||Rock- If you produce them, put me on the list as a buyer.<P>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000025||rockcrawl||08-16-2000||07:07 PM||||Thanks for all the feedback! I will consider making one for the other side. My thought was that Pontiac only put it on one side, so thats how I'm going to do it. Some say Pontiac left the right one off to cut costs, but there was really no reason to have one on the other side. I designed this scoop to be a sort of alternative to the Holley air scoop. It will have a mounting flange around the inner edges on the back, so for those that want to remove the quarter panel and screw it on, you can. Any comments on having two recessed screw holes that line up with the original vent screw holes (like the holley scoop)? This would allow screw mounting without removing the quarter, but would mean having two holes in the surface of the scoop. I had made a smaller one that lined up with the body lines, but it was too small and restrictive. I will be making some larger bolt-on scoops(both sides) with Mecham styling, but the stumbling point is hiding the original body lines of the air intake without replacing the entire quarter panel. <P>Thanks again for all the input. At this point I probably will not be making a matching one for the other side. I'd rather spend the time designing a pair of larger scoops. I think most of you who want a scoop on both sides would also rather have larger scoops. I'm currently waiting for a shipment of supplies so I can continue.||||reg||12
