Z||000032||BellaFiero||08-17-2000||10:11 AM||||Very sweet! I like it alot... count me in! That's decent of you to make a scoop for each side,  I think it will look very cool with twins coops. Where did you get the idea for the shape? It kind of looks like a Cobra Mini-Jet ( which :: buffs his knuckles on his shirt :: I happen to have installed on my baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )scoop. How long does it take to produce the scoop? Any projected cost, and ship date? You shouldn't have told us about it yet, because I think you'll be swamped with orders before you even make another ONE!<BR>A very cool mod, and one that I am very interested in!<P>------------------<BR>"No, no... you can't put that there, it'll be in the way of the Johnson Rod!"  ||||reg||14
Z||000033||Bill Osmer||08-17-2000||11:03 AM||||Rockcrawler -<BR>Good work at coming up with the design. Some of this thread asks how to "hide" the driver's side indent - why not think of adding a surface to the opening where a rigid screen could be mounted (by the purchaser)? That way, it would serve as a visual "block" as well as keeping debri out of the intake side. I think if you check a previous thread about another scoop, you'll see an example of a screen addition.<P>BTW - put me on the list (although I really lust after "Mecham-style" scoops - can't they be surface mounted, too?)<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
