Z||000046||rockcrawl||08-21-2000||03:49 PM||||Formula, I'll be putting two on my '87 without cutting a hole in the pass side quarter panel. I'm not even going to use screws to attach them, only the double sided tape. I'll give them the 120 MPH test and see if they hang in there or if they blow off.<P>DXR, I'm kinda prepared to handle the situation if I can't keep up with demand. No, I'm not building a factory! There is a reputable Kit-Car manufacturer about 15 minutes from where I live, In fact I bought my Countach and Testarossa bodies there. He currently makes all the ground effects and wings for the local Rice-Boy shop, so I'm thinking maybe I can take him my molds and have him make the scoops if I don't have the time. Like I said, I'll try to make enough for everyone here. <P>The molds for both sides are done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, and I'll be starting to make scoops this week. The most I can do are two per day (night).<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000047||Blade||08-21-2000||07:57 PM||||Do these scoops increase performance. or are they a cooling thing. If they increase peformance how much and or how much do they cool..ect.<BR>Im new to the fieros i wont have mine for another week but im lookin to fix it up.<P>Blade||||reg||1
